01:31:53.174 --> 01:31:54.609
I mean a soulless plant.

01:31:54.609 --> 01:31:55.910
I'm like, I've never even voted.

01:31:55.910 --> 01:31:58.679
Like I literally prior
to getting into things

01:31:58.679 --> 01:32:01.749 align:start size:88% position:13%
I genuinely just was not
politically inclined.

01:32:01.749 --> 01:32:03.518
And I just thought I
had to be a Democrat

01:32:03.518 --> 01:32:04.719
and thought I had
to be a liberal.

01:32:04.719 --> 01:32:06.687 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, you know, looking
in the retrospect,

01:32:06.687 --> 01:32:08.923 align:start size:84% position:16%
I realized how foolish
that is, you know,

01:32:08.923 --> 01:32:11.158
that I didn't realize that
everything was really...

01:32:11.158 --> 01:32:12.994
That everything that
bad happened in my life

01:32:12.994 --> 01:32:17.131 align:start size:97% position:3%
was really routed to bad
policies and bad politicians.

01:32:17.131 --> 01:32:19.667
But I wanted to first lay
out just my personal story.

01:32:19.667 --> 01:32:20.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, the subtitle
of the book is

01:32:20.902 --> 01:32:23.538
"How Black America Can
Make it's Second Escape

01:32:23.538 --> 01:32:25.873
"From the Democrat Plantations."

01:32:25.873 --> 01:32:28.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I do believe, I
say this all the time,

01:32:28.376 --> 01:32:29.610
people get upset,

01:32:29.610 --> 01:32:32.013 align:start size:88% position:13%
that black Americans are
still enslaved today,

01:32:32.013 --> 01:32:33.481
that the Left just got smarter.

01:32:33.481 --> 01:32:36.517
And they realized that
you can't enslave people,

01:32:36.517 --> 01:32:39.186
their bodies, you can't
have black Americans

01:32:39.186 --> 01:32:40.721
on the plantation anymore,

01:32:40.721 --> 01:32:42.490
but you can still have black
Americans doing all the work

01:32:42.490 --> 01:32:44.358
for you and reaping no benefit.

01:32:44.358 --> 01:32:45.826 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that is a structure
that we see today

01:32:45.826 --> 01:32:47.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
between black America
and the Democratic Party.

01:32:47.862 --> 01:32:49.063
We are doing all the work,

01:32:49.063 --> 01:32:50.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
we carried them
over the finish line

01:32:50.998 --> 01:32:53.701
and we benefit not
in one single way.

01:32:53.701 --> 01:32:56.404
And so I really kind of
lay out that argument

01:32:56.404 --> 01:32:59.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and talk about what slave
life was really like,

01:32:59.473 --> 01:33:00.942
the breakdown of family,

01:33:00.942 --> 01:33:02.877
why it was necessary for
families to be broken down,

01:33:02.877 --> 01:33:05.346
to trade constantly
be trading slaves

01:33:05.346 --> 01:33:07.582
from one plantation to
the next to the next,

01:33:07.582 --> 01:33:09.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
they could have no
feelings for one another.

01:33:09.984 --> 01:33:12.620
And Frederick Douglas
in his autobiography,

01:33:12.620 --> 01:33:14.088
the first couple of pages,

01:33:14.088 --> 01:33:15.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he starts talking
about his life as a slave.

01:33:15.990 --> 01:33:17.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
He talks about the fact
that when his mother died,

01:33:17.558 --> 01:33:18.793
he felt nothing.

01:33:18.793 --> 01:33:20.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
When the sisters were
traded, he felt nothing,

01:33:20.795 --> 01:33:22.930
he had no sense of kinship.

01:33:22.930 --> 01:33:25.700
No familial love
for his own blood.

01:33:25.700 --> 01:33:27.935
That was necessary to the
institution of slavery.

01:33:27.935 --> 01:33:30.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
We still have that kinship
and that relationship

01:33:30.004 --> 01:33:32.340
and that community
still broken down

01:33:32.340 --> 01:33:33.808
all of these years later,

01:33:33.808 --> 01:33:36.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
despite the reconstruction
era post-slavery,

01:33:36.577 --> 01:33:39.046 align:start position:0%
which we saw black American
families getting back together,

01:33:39.046 --> 01:33:40.915
we were doing something.

01:33:40.915 --> 01:33:42.450
It's all been wiped away.

01:33:42.450 --> 01:33:44.986
- At a higher rate, by the
way, until about 72 or so.

01:33:44.986 --> 01:33:48.789 align:start position:0%
- In the 1950S, black
Americans were outpacing whites

01:33:48.789 --> 01:33:50.391
in terms of economic growth.

01:33:50.391 --> 01:33:53.427
And then immediately
following, the 1960s

01:33:53.427 --> 01:33:56.731 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the Great Society Act
and the systemic oppression,

01:33:56.731 --> 01:33:58.366
which started via
the welfare system,

01:33:58.366 --> 01:34:00.101 align:start size:81% position:19%
everything started
falling apart.

01:34:00.101 --> 01:34:04.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
And reading another topic,
going back to slavery.

01:34:04.839 --> 01:34:07.074 align:start size:97% position:3%
Black Americans, it was
illegal for black Americans

01:34:07.074 --> 01:34:08.542
to learn how to read.

01:34:08.542 --> 01:34:10.378 align:start position:0%
In fact, it was so illegal that
if you were a white person,

01:34:10.378 --> 01:34:14.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you were caught
teaching your slave to read,

01:34:14.382 --> 01:34:17.018
you would be found guilty
too, it was a serious sin.

01:34:17.018 --> 01:34:19.587
The reason for that is because
they didn't want Black people

01:34:19.587 --> 01:34:22.289 align:start position:0%
being educated because an
educated mind can't be enslaved.

01:34:22.289 --> 01:34:23.724
Well, what's changed?

01:34:23.724 --> 01:34:25.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
And look at the literacy
rates in black America today.

01:34:25.726 --> 01:34:27.328
Look at Baltimore, look
at the inner cities.

01:34:27.328 --> 01:34:29.030
Look at we're in California.

01:34:29.030 --> 01:34:32.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
At California, 70% of
black boys could not pass

01:34:32.233 --> 01:34:33.801
the basic literacy exam.

01:34:33.801 --> 01:34:35.403
Nobody's talking about that.

01:34:35.403 --> 01:34:37.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have politicians that
are standing on stage

01:34:37.471 --> 01:34:39.740
saying that all they care
about is black Americans.

01:34:39.740 --> 01:34:41.642
They're not talking
about everything

01:34:41.642 --> 01:34:43.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is harming black
Americans today.

01:34:43.310 --> 01:34:46.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everything that is recreating
the very same plantations

01:34:46.814 --> 01:34:48.182
that we came from.

01:34:48.182 --> 01:34:49.617 align:start size:97% position:3%
